OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F315A1787006889
OL,3,C'Gel nail ban': What are the new rules?
OL,5,FWhat is the "gel nail ban"?
OL,7,FAlthough branded a "gel nail ban", the
OL,8,Fban only refers to one specific
OL,9,Fingredient known as trimethylbenzoyl
OL,10,Fdiphenylphosphine oxide, or TPO.
OL,12,FTPO is a "photoinitiator", which means
OL,13,Fit starts the chemical reaction to
OL,14,Fallow gel polish to cure under
OL,15,Fultraviolet (UV) light, giving the
OL,16,Fmanicured nails that glossy appearance
OL,17,Fand durable surface.
OL,19,FWhen does the ban come into effect?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
